Package: libcamera-loopback
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Alan Velasco <dev@alanbato.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, kmod
Suggests: v4l2loopback-dkms, gstreamer1.0-libcamera
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/alanbato/libcamera-loopback
Description: on-demand libcamera to v4l2loopback webcam relay
 Feeds a v4l2loopback device from a libcamera camera (via GStreamer's
 libcamerasrc), so that browsers, video-call apps and PipeWire can use MIPI
 laptop cameras, such as those on Intel IPU6 laptops, like a regular webcam.
 The camera is only started while an application is reading from the device.
 .
 It is a drop-in replacement for v4l2-relayd that writes frames with write(),
 which avoids crashes and frozen video in applications reading from the
 loopback device. If v4l2-relayd is installed, its default instance is masked
 while this package is installed.
 .
 Requires the v4l2loopback kernel module and a libcamera with the software
 ISP and its GStreamer plugin. Ubuntu 24.04's libcamera is too old for IPU6;
 see /usr/share/doc/libcamera-loopback/README.md for building a newer one.
